{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Create a new external Go module/repository named fabric-lib-go (as suggested in U5) with sub-packages protoutil, bccsp, msp and discovery client; use semantic versioning with v1 tags and consume it from fabric core via go.mod.",
    "Preserve the existing exported APIs of protoutil, bccsp, msp and the discovery client so that fabric-sdk-go can delete its internal copies and consume fabric-lib-go as a drop-in replacement.",
    "U1: replace the cauthdsl/protoutil usage in core/chaincode/shim/ext/statebased with a small local constructor for signature policy envelopes built directly on fabric-protos-go types, so the only remaining fabric imports are the protos.",
    "U2: reimplement the entities package encryption using Go standard library crypto (crypto/aes, crypto/cipher, crypto/rand) behind the unchanged public API, dropping the bccsp and flogging imports entirely.",
    "Eliminate flogging from all externalized code: remove logging calls or fall back to the standard library log package to avoid dragging fabric logging dependencies into consumers.",
    "Where externalized packages still need fabric-internal behavior (e.g., identity handling pulled in via protoutil), define narrow local interfaces or localize the helpers instead of importing fabric core packages, breaking the transitive dependency chains.",
    "Add CI dependency-guard jobs that run 'go list -f {{join .Deps \"\" \"\\n\"}}' checks for the shim/ext packages so the U1/U2 acceptance criteria are enforced permanently.",
    "Keep PKCS#11 support in the externalized bccsp behind build tags with SoftHSM-based CI tests, so the default build has no cgo/HSM requirement.",
    "Sequence the single-developer delivery as: dependency analysis -> shim/ext cleanups (U1, U2) -> samples fix (U3/U4) -> fabric-lib-go scaffolding -> protoutil -> bccsp -> msp -> discovery client -> fabric core integration -> SDK validation -> documentation."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The code base is Hyperledger Fabric v2.x using Go modules, and fabric-protos-go is already externalized and available as a dependency (implied by U5).",
    "Repository creation, CI infrastructure and maintainer rights for the new fabric-lib-go repository are available at no additional setup cost beyond the scaffolding activity estimated here.",
    "U3 and U4 describe the same fabric-samples change for marbles02_private and are implemented once; their effort is not double-counted.",
    "Estimates cover all development work personally performed: analysis, design, coding, unit tests, code-review iterations, CI setup and verification; they represent effort in work-hours, not elapsed calendar duration.",
    "Acceptance for U1 and U2 is verified by scripted 'go list' dependency checks executed locally and added to CI.",
    "U8 covers only the client-side discovery packages; the peer-side discovery service remains in fabric core.",
    "Idemix remains in fabric core for this increment; the externalized bccsp does not require idemix, matching what the Go SDK actually vendors.",
    "No changes to fabric-sdk-go are in scope beyond a validation branch; SDK maintainers perform their own final migration.",
    "PKCS#11 testing uses SoftHSM in CI; no physical HSM is required.",
    "Existing fabric unit and integration (e2e) test suites are available and runnable in CI for the integration activity."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Dependency analysis and target design",
      "activity_description": "Run go list dependency analysis for statebased, entities and the client-facing packages; map the transitive dependency chains (cauthdsl, protoutil, internal/pkg/identity, bccsp, flogging); design the fabric-lib-go module layout, the dependency-guard approach and the API-compatibility strategy.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "U1: statebased dependency cleanup",
      "activity_description": "Refactor core/chaincode/shim/ext/statebased to eliminate imports of common/cauthdsl and protoutil by implementing a minimal local signature-policy-envelope constructor on fabric-protos-go types; update and extend unit tests; verify acceptance with go list and wire the dependency-guard check.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U2: entities dependency cleanup",
      "activity_description": "Refactor core/chaincode/shim/ext/entities to drop bccsp and flogging by reimplementing the AES encryption with Go standard library crypto behind the existing public API; update unit tests including known-answer vectors; verify acceptance with go list.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U3/U4: marbles02_private samples fix",
      "activity_description": "Update the marbles02_private chaincode in fabric-samples: add the suggested comment and append '| tr -d \\n' to the base64 export examples to prevent line-wrap JSON parsing errors on Windows-hosted virtual environments; update the README; validate the commands on Ubuntu VM and macOS; shepherd the PR.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "fabric-lib-go repository scaffolding",
      "activity_description": "Bootstrap the fabric-lib-go repository: LICENSE/NOTICE/SECURITY/MAINTAINERS files, Go module definition, branching and semantic-versioning policy, CI pipeline (build, unit tests, lint, dependency-guard job) and initial README/contribution documentation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U5: externalize protoutil",
      "activity_description": "Audit the protoutil sources; decouple them from internal/pkg/identity, flogging, common/crypto and other fabric-internal packages by localizing helpers or injecting narrow interfaces; move code and unit tests into fabric-lib-go keeping the exported API drop-in compatible; review the API surface; reach green CI and tag v1.0.0.",
      "most_likely_effort": 120
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U6: externalize BCCSP",
      "activity_description": "Move bccsp core, factory, signer, sw and utils into fabric-lib-go with the pkcs11 provider behind a build tag (tested via SoftHSM); decouple from flogging/metrics via minimal interfaces; port the test suite; verify drop-in compatibility against the SDK's vendored copy; tag a release.",
      "most_likely_effort": 96
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U7: externalize MSP",
      "activity_description": "Move the msp package into fabric-lib-go on top of the externalized bccsp and fabric-protos-go; decouple from cauthdsl/policies/flogging by localizing required helpers and defining narrow interfaces; port identity (de)serialization and validation tests; tag a release.",
      "most_likely_effort": 120
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "U8: externalize discovery client",
      "activity_description": "Move the client-side discovery packages (client, endorsement and peer-selection logic) into fabric-lib-go; decouple from gossip/comm by defining local gRPC/TLS abstractions; add mocked-server unit tests; tag a release.",
      "most_likely_effort": 80
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Fabric core integration",
      "activity_description": "Update fabric core to consume fabric-lib-go: adjust go.mod requirements, replace in-repo packages with imports from the external module, delete superseded internal copies, fix compilation fallout, and run the fabric unit and integration (e2e) suites resolving any failures.",
      "most_likely_effort": 48
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Downstream (SDK) consumption validation",
      "activity_description": "Build a small sample client exercising protoutil, bccsp, msp and discovery from fabric-lib-go; verify on a test branch that fabric-sdk-go can replace its internal copies; record API gaps and apply fixes.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "Documentation and release support",
      "activity_description": "Polish godoc, write fabric-lib-go READMEs and a migration guide, produce release notes, and update fabric documentation that references the moved packages.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 588
  }
}

